WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.500
Good morning John.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.000
Amsterdam is very good,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.780
I wanna have a lot of different thoughts from this place.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.280
Thoughts about tulips,

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.560
and financialization,

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.380
and economic bubbles and genetics.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.320
Thoughts about how some clogs seemed quite big

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.960
until I saw others, and then

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.640
...This....Wow!

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.380
Thoughts about how there's a freaking fair in the middle

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.460
of this town right now

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.420
sharing space with 400 - 500 year old buildings

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.140
and fair food is pretty much the same everywhere.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.900
"I asked for American sauce

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.060
because I figured it would be ranch dressing...

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.120
but it's not.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.620
I do not know this flavor."

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.080
But of all the thoughts I could have from this place,

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.860
guess what I spotted while casually Google mapping around

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.000
to see what there was to do....

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.840
Oh ... a bench.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.300
The Fault in Our Stars Bench,

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.200
on Google Maps, with 75 reviews,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.720
and an average rating of 4.3,

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.280
which is just as good as the Van Gogh Museum.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:03.940
John,

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.360
I assume that you are equally as fascinated

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.880
to find out what people say, when they review a bench.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.320
Which is why this video is going to be mostly people's reviews of the TFiOS bench.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.420
"It’s just a bench!"

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.400
"It’s a bench!"

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.360
"Honestly, it’s just an ordinary bench."

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.660
Though apparently that was worth four stars.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:22.460
"It’s...

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:23.880
bench.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:24.600
That’s it."

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.400
Some don’t even think that it’s a particularly good bench.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.440
Milena, in a two star review says

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.080
it’s extremely uncomfortable and she doesn’t know how Hazel and Gus did it

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.860
and Dominika remarks on the bench’s aesthetic, I think, more than its cleanliness

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.700
when she says that people need to treat it better.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.840
It does appear to be the opposite of the largest ball of paint,

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.580
in that many tourists seem to remove paint every time they go, rather than add it.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.520
But of course, there are lots of great reviews of the bench.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.880
Marciano says that there are a few promise locks

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.960
which have apparently multiplied substantially in the last 8 months

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.380
because this is more than a few.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.940
Maharlika says that it was really fun to try to recreate the famous movie poster

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.080
and suggests that you take a picture from the other side of the canal,

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.320
which is how they did it in the movie.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.520
That is an excellent tip!

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.500
Katarina deeply disagrees with all those remarking on the bench’s lack of comfort

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.940
saying: "10/10 Would sit again".

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.560
Joanna agrees saying, best free attraction in Amsterdam,

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.380
visited twice in one day, five stars.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.440
Though to be fair, there are no other free attractions in Amsterdam.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.420
Now, none of these reviews really encapsulated my experience with the bench,

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.500
so John, I left my own review.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:31.820
Here it is:

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:35.400
"My brother wrote a book, that made a bench, famous enough that is has seventy-five,

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.860
now seventy-six reviews on Google.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.320
That’s really weird, and also amazing.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.540
If you’re just wandering around Amsterdam,

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.420
there’s a pretty good chance that you’re going to accidentally come across this bench.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.580
It’s a fine bench, but ultimately, it’s just a bench that is in no way special,

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.140
except because of what people bring to it.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:55.160
I guess that’s like most important things, and also people.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.740
We aren’t much, unless you know our story.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.760
I sat by this bench for a long time watching people come up and take pictures with the bench,

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.400
some of them didn’t seem to care that much and were just looking for something to do between events

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:10.840
but others were clearly excited to interact a bit with a physical space that was important to them,

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.780
or to their relationships.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.220
There were a lot of friend groups and a lot of couples.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.480
It made me happy.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.800
My brother is a little bit obsessed with road side attractions in America

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:28.340
and it is very cool and very weird that he unintentionally inspired a canal-side attraction across an ocean.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.340
Each person brings to this thing

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.680
their own stories and their own connections.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:34.860
Each person

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.740
makes it a little bit more

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.320
than it was ever meant to be.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:39.180
Again,

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.780
maybe, a little bit like all of us.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:42.400
John,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.800
I’ll see you on Tuesday."

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.120
(all): Good morning, Hank it’s Tuesday!

